WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.898
Could you go from an idea to a business, in one conversation?

2
00:00:05.148 --> 00:00:10.555
I'm a dog groomer, and I want to go mobile. I tell Cunning Claw the idea.

3
00:00:10.805 --> 00:00:19.086
It shapes it. Who it's for, three services, prices. Every figure marked as a guess, for me to check.

4
00:00:19.336 --> 00:00:21.452
Next, the business plan.

5
00:00:21.702 --> 00:00:24.392
It asks before it runs anything.

6
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.708
It writes the plan, and prints it.

7
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.268
Start-up costs, the first year, the risks. All mine to check.

8
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.353
Now the website. It hands that to Claude Code.

9
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.586
Here's the brief, word for word. Nothing starts until I say so.

10
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.241
Claude Code builds it, on its own branch. Under a minute.

11
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.054
Then the claw reports back, and opens the site right beside our chat.

12
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.718
Services and prices, straight from the plan.

13
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.047
A booking form that checks every answer.

14
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.802
And it works on a phone.

15
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.764
Last, the launch material. A flyer, three posts, and an email.

16
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.654
The first flyer is a bit plain. So I say so.

17
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.266
It reads the website's colours, and designs it properly.

18
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.961
Replacing my file? It asks first.

19
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.746
That's more like it.

20
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.989
Three posts and a launch email. Drafts. Nothing sent.

21
00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:17.430
An idea, a plan, a website, and the marketing. For less than a dollar.

22
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:24.566
Cunning Claw. It does the legwork. You say yes. Free, at cunningclaw.com.
